course: dictionary
lesson: 11239
title: Workplace and where people work
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A workplace is the place where people go to do their job. The words around it give you clues. «The Arsenal of Venice was a huge state shipyard that could build ships one after another, almost like a factory» tells you that people worked there building ships, so it was a workplace.
explain: Read the sentence again and ask: what word would fit here? «A picket line is striking workers standing outside their workplace with signs» shows workers standing outside the place where they work. So workplace means the place where you do your job.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it. «Smoking is banned inside workplaces and pubs» becomes «banned inside places where people go to do their job and pubs», and that still makes sense. Your meaning works, so you can trust it.
fact: A workplace is a place where people go to do their job.
fact: Offices, factories, shops and schools are all workplaces.
fact: A workplace can be big, like a huge shipyard, or small, like a corner shop.
fact: Workplaces often have rules to keep workers safe, such as fire exits and safety signs.
fact: «Workplace» is a noun, and it can be plural: workplaces.
exercise: «A picket line is striking workers standing outside their workplace with signs.» Where do the workers stand? | On a boat far out at sea | *Outside the place where they do their job | In a park with their friends | At home in bed
exercise: Mum says, «My workplace is an office on the fifth floor.» What is a workplace? | *A place where people go to do their job | A bus stop | A place where people go to play games | A type of weather
exercise: Which of these is a workplace? | A dog's basket | A puddle after the rain | A park where children play | *A factory where people make cars
test: «Smoking is banned inside workplaces and pubs.» What does workplaces mean? | Places where people go to sleep | Places where people grow food in gardens | *Places where people go to do their job | Places where animals live
test: Which of these is the best example of a workplace? | *A school where teachers teach | A bench in the park for picnics | A pond where ducks swim | A field where cows graze
exam: Jayden says a workplace is only an office. Is he right? | *No, a factory, a shop or a school can be a workplace too | Yes, only offices are workplaces | No, only homes are workplaces | Yes, only shops are workplaces
